1
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,800
There's bound to be something.

2
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,940
Anyone without work, come to me.

3
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:04,500
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

4
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,560
Look, it's on fire!

5
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:11,940
Akaneru too.

6
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:21,540
You get it, right?

8
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,500
I get it, I get it.

9
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,440
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

10
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,480
Ryo-san's Double Face

11
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:55,380
What's wrong, senior?

12
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:56,880
What's the problem?

13
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,380
It's this article in this magazine.

14
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:01,640
Whether they're hunks or whatever,
I don't know.

15
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:04,940
What does playing sports have
to do with having a good face?

16
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:08,700
That? Well,
handsome guys do get lots of fans, right?

17
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:12,180
Some of them are practically TV celebrities.

18
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:13,040
Outrageous!

19
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:17,720
Being good at sports and having a good face
are totally different things to begin with.

20
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:21,180
Just because they're good-looking, they get
pampered by fans and their form drops off.

21
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,920
What happens if they stop
putting their heart into sports?

22
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:25,060
W-well, honestly!

23
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:26,940
That's true, but...

24
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,820
They're athletes, so rather than
whether they're good-looking or not,

25
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:33,660
there should be much,
much more important things.

26
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:36,560
Whether someone is good-looking
has nothing to do with sports at all.

27
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:39,000
Absolutely no connection whatsoever.

28
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:42,740
A person isn't defined by their face,
after all.

29
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:44,780
what that person has actually done,

30
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:47,260
how much skill they really have.

31
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:48,480
That's what matters.

32
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:51,220
I suppose what you're
saying is the right argument,

33
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:54,200
but coming from Ryo-chan,
it just somehow doesn't sound right.

34
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,600
Bo-bo...

35
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:59,460
We are the Young Detective Corps!

36
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:05,540
Gentlemen, it's been a while!

37
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,720
Professor Esaki.

38
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:10,320
You've been dressing up in cosplay lately

39
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:13,040
At your age,
what's the idea of dressing like that?

40
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:15,280
Isn't it obvious, Gorilla-kun?

41
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,360
I am the...

42
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:20,520
Fiend with Twenty Faces!

43
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:30,440
We are the Boy Detective Corps

44
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:33,920
Yuuki rin-rin-rin-rin-rin-rin

45
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,540
The song's different partway through,
isn't it?

46
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:38,060
That's Finger Five.

47
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:42,160
Anyway, why would the Fiend with Twenty
Faces be singing the Boy Detectives' song?

48
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:45,020
Don't sweat the small stuff.

49
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:46,620
Here, I'll give you this.

50
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:50,380
This is a BD badge.

51
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:57,100
That's why the BD badge belongs to the Boy Detectives,
and the Fiend with Twenty Faces doesn't have one, you idiot.

52
00:03:57,100 --> 00:04:00,080
The topic's too niche, I can't keep up.

53
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:01,240
Me too.

54
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:03,720
By the way,
what did you come here for today?

55
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:09,600
You pretended to be a sleepwalker, so this must have
something to do with the Twenty Faces villain, right?

56
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:15,520
It's my theory, Gorilla-kun! My super brain has made an unprecedented,
world-first invention,

57
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:18,060
a truly great invention!

58
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:23,700
Amazing... the pervert mask!

59
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:27,700
What happens when you put
this mask on your face is...

60
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:29,440
What's wrong?

61
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:31,680
What is this?

62
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:34,720
It's stuck on tight.
You can't get it off at all!

63
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:37,780
What do I do?

64
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,280
No problem.

65
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,686
Like this, like this,

66
00:04:44,736 --> 00:04:47,780
and when you do this, voilà, how amazing!

67
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:53,820
What? It looks just like the Chief!

68
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,480
Don't be surprised just yet.

69
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:04,560
Now, if I do it like this,
and like this, and like this...

70
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:07,940
This time it's the Chief, isn't it?

71
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:08,840
I see.

72
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:13,460
With this pervert mask on,
you can make any face you like.

73
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:16,280
Gorilla-kun, from now on you'll have 20 faces...
no, 20 times that.

74
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,540
No, you'll have 200 times as many faces!

75
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:22,120
You've become a five-faced pervert,
you know.

76
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,540
This actually sounds kind of fun.

77
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:29,540
Let's see, like this...

78
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:32,680
If you do it that way, and then this...

79
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,400
That's Reiko, right?

80
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:40,020
Stop it, that's creepy!

81
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:42,060
That flat-top is creepy.

82
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:46,480
By the way, how do I get this mask off?

83
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:54,040
That's for another time.

84
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:57,340
What do you mean, "another time"?

85
00:05:57,340 --> 00:06:00,560
It means you can look forward
to it until we meet next time.

86
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:06,200
Farewell, modern district!

87
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:09,360
If you're going to say that, it should be
"Akechi-kun," you idiot.

88
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:13,220
Damn it,
what are you going to do about this face?

89
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:19,220
As usual,
you're irresponsible and one-sided.

90
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:23,400
I bet he still doesn't know
how to take the mask off.

91
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,600
Yeah, I bet that's it.

92
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:26,400
Nakagawa-san.

93
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:30,580
What do you want with me, ladies?

94
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:34,420
Nakagawa-san, are you free next Sunday?

95
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:36,240
Want to go for a drive together?

96
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:40,080
Yeah, in my specially built Ferrari,

97
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:42,080
racing through Wangan Midnight,

98
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:45,100
shall we all have some dawn coffee?

99
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:47,760
Stylish!

100
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:49,220
As if that'd ever happen.

101
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:52,480
You perverted gorilla, Ryotsu.

102
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:55,680
I guess you can't fool people
with just a face after all.

103
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,980
Of course not.

104
00:06:57,520 --> 00:07:00,200
I just pretended to go
along with it for a bit.

105
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:03,760
What on earth are you doing,
copying Nakagawa's face like that?

106
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:06,360
You'll tarnish Nakagawa's good looks!

107
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:09,500
It's Ryo-chan's new toy.

108
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:14,080
Senpai, please, I'm begging you,
stop turning into my face.

109
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:16,400
I thought I transformed pretty well, though.

110
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:18,220
Worst.

111
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,560
Can I have a word?

112
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:30,600
I have a special assignment for you.

113
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:32,520
Special assignment?

114
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:36,900
Yes, starting today you've been assigned
to the Special Investigation Division.

115
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:39,740
Special Investigation Division?

116
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:44,080
That's right.
There's no one else suited for it but you.

117
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:48,160
But I'm not special in any way.

118
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:49,040
Yes you are.

119
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:52,620
You may not realize it yourself,

120
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:54,800
but you're a remarkably special person.

121
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:57,780
It's that stubbornness of yours.

122
00:07:57,780 --> 00:08:01,740
So from today, you'll go by the name
"Fundoshi Deka."

123
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:03,880
"Fundoshi Deka"?

124
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:07,720
What does being stubborn
have to do with a fundoshi?

125
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:10,240
When it comes to stubbornness,
it's the stubborn old father,

126
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:13,060
and the symbol of the stubborn old father

127
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:15,700
is always the fundoshi, isn't it?

128
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:19,300
We secretly conducted a survey
of prefectural police nationwide,

129
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:21,760
and among all the police officers in Japan,

130
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:25,440
the results show that you are the
one who suits the fundoshi best.

131
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:29,520
You wouldn't dare say you refuse, would you?

132
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:31,700
W-well, that's...

133
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:35,660
Then hurry up and change into your uniform.

134
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,500
Is this all right?

135
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:49,940
Well, I suppose it'll do.

136
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:54,340
But a special investigator should
not be embarrassed like this.

137
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:56,940
Hold yourself up with dignity!

138
00:08:56,940 --> 00:09:03,940
But with just this outfit, it still doesn't
quite feel like a special investigator.

139
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:09,280
Shall we liven things up with the usual entrance scene,
with the factory-style fanfare?

140
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:12,080
Ha ha ha

141
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,080
Yes, yes!

142
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:21,280
With his red fundoshi fluttering,
that man has come to town.

143
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:25,340
Drifting, drifting,
a lone wandering man, a crow on the road.

144
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:28,460
Metropolitan Police Special Investigation Unit,
Daijirō Ohara.

145
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:29,600
Known to all as...

146
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,800
Fundoshi Deka.

147
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,480
You're starting to get the feel of it.

148
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:42,500
But your movements still lack sharpness.

149
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:44,580
When you spin, do it with all your might.

150
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:49,100
You need to turn about this much.

151
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:49,820
Yes.

152
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:52,680
And the all-important
finishing pose is like this.

153
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:56,420
Raise your right elbow properly
and stretch your legs out fully.

154
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:57,480
Yes.

155
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:01,520
Practice here for a while.

156
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:06,740
Once you can do it properly,

157
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:08,980
come to my office and show me.

158
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:09,660
Y-yes!

159
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:12,060
If you can't do this properly,

160
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:14,460
in this era of layoffs, your path in life

161
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:17,540
will be extremely harsh, understand?

162
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:18,440
Yes.

163
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:20,500
Then I'll look forward to it.

164
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:21,600
I'll be waiting.

165
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:39,580
It's Ohara.

166
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:40,880
Come in.

167
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,340
Excuse me.

168
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:48,040
Ohara-kun.

169
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,040
Chief, please watch me.

170
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:53,540
This time I'll nail it perfectly.

171
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,580
With a red fundoshi fluttering,
he came to town.

172
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:06,840
Drifting, drifting,
a lone wandering man, a traveling drifter.

173
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:09,860
Metropolitan Police Special Crimes Division,
Daijiro Ohara.

174
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:12,700
They call him Fundoshi Deka.

175
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,780
How about this? Just a moment.

176
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:18,720
Will this collar connect to mine?

177
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:26,760
Chief Ohara is giving all of
this to Ryo-san as a present?

178
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:30,160
He actually did something
worthy of praise for once.

179
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:32,860
So put the bill on my tab.

180
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:33,460
Yes.

181
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:34,460
Thank you for your order!

182
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:37,580
Ten servings of premium sushi,
charge it to me.

183
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:39,940
Five ramen and eight fried rice.

184
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:41,580
And eight servings of gyoza.

185
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:44,080
Put all of it on my tab.

186
00:11:53,660 --> 00:11:56,440
Thanks to this mask, this is heaven.

187
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,900
I look just like the Chief,
if I do say so myself.

188
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:02,500
So who should I transform into tomorrow?

189
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:07,440
I'll think about that tomorrow.

190
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:14,540
Mm.

191
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:17,580
Mm. Mm.

192
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:26,340
Oh no, I'm late again.
I should come up with a good excuse.

193
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:27,760
Hey.

194
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:36,520
Right, where's my uniform? There it is.

195
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:47,580
Good morning.

196
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,600
Why are you so surprised?

197
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:55,100
I wonder when that guy joined.

198
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:10,580
Somehow I feel like
everyone's staring at me.

199
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:15,740
Good morning!

200
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:18,620
What's with that reaction?

201
00:13:19,140 --> 00:13:20,880
Is that you, Ryo-chan?

202
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:21,980
Who else would it be?

203
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:26,180
Spy, what happened to your face?

204
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:27,600
Face?

205
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:30,380
Try to calm down.

206
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:32,100
What?

207
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:38,420
So this is my face?

208
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:53,280
Damn, so that's why everyone
was staring at my face in shock.

209
00:13:58,040 --> 00:13:59,600
What happened to you?

210
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,800
My face won't change shape.

211
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:06,520
It's gone rock-hard, like a rice cake.

212
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:12,320
After all,
it's one of Professor Esaki's inventions.

213
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,520
That Esaki guy!

214
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,280
Pa-row everybody!

215
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:20,140
Esaki, you bastard,
what is the meaning of this?

216
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:22,900
Pa!

217
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,000
It's not "pa," you idiot, it's not "pa"!

218
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:29,580
I'm asking why my face turned
into this and hardened like this!

219
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:32,940
It'll be about two or three hours.

220
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:34,780
What's two or three hours?

221
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:41,760
In two or three hours it'll harden completely,
then peel right off like a scab, pororiin, Gorilla-kun.

222
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:43,600
Well then, until then.

223
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:46,280
Wait with that face for a while, won't you.

224
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,040
Farewell, Homudokku!

225
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:54,580
What on earth did he come here for?

226
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:58,800
But will it really peel
off in two or three hours?

227
00:14:59,160 --> 00:14:59,600
Well...

228
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:06,860
Well then, Senpai,
please take care of the night shift.

229
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:10,440
You'd better not show yourself
in front of people too much.

230
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:13,680
It's bad for the heart of anyone
seeing you for the first time.

231
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:16,860
And please don't cause
any weird commotion, okay?

232
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:17,920
I know, I know.

233
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:21,000
Damn, today was the night shift

234
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,580
But this mask just won't come off at all!

235
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:35,440
Excuse me, is the newlywed
Amano family's house around here?

236
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,360
What?

237
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:41,580
Help!

238
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:48,880
Judging people by their faces

239
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:54,360
Even so, that's pretty amazing,
I have to say.

240
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:08,600
It's gotten dark and it
still won't come off at all.

241
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:14,700
I'll just stay like this until my face goes back.
I'm starving.

242
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:19,660
Come to think of it,
I haven't eaten a thing since last night.

243
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:29,440
There's nothing here, damn it.
Guess I'll go out and buy some food.

244
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:36,720
If I leave the place empty and it gets robbed,
that'd be a disaster.

245
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:38,900
At least I'll take my handgun with me.

246
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:41,680
Someone's here.

247
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:44,412
What the hell?

248
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:51,420
That punk's talking to me like he's my equal,
the bastard.

249
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:52,960
Because a call came in,

250
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,600
I shut him out.

251
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:57,040
I went and beat that guy to a pulp,
you know.

252
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:30,340
!

253
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,340
S-sorry! Please, go ahead!

254
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:34,640
You're letting me go first?

255
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:36,640
P-please, please!

256
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:37,560
Thank you very much.

257
